.\" The man page the APT and DNF packages install. Their packslip is built
.\" with --features install-cli, so it has no publishing commands. Written by
.\" hand: keep it in step with the install, verify, pin, show, and completion
.\" help in src/main.rs.
.TH PACKSLIP 1 "October 2026" "packslip" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
packslip \- install and verify signed upstream releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B packslip install
.I PROJECT
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B packslip verify
.I BUNDLE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B packslip pin
.I BUNDLE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B packslip show
.I BUNDLE
.RB [ \-\-raw ]
.br
.B packslip completion
.I SHELL
.br
.B packslip version
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B packslip install
finds a project's release, verifies its release bundle and the artifact for
this host, and unpacks the archive into an installation tree.
It exports only the commands the release declares.
It runs no downloaded code, installs no dependencies, and edits no shell
configuration.
There is no uninstall, upgrade, or list.
.PP
The packslip in this package installs and verifies releases.
The release binaries add create, keygen, releases, and schema, which publish
releases; see https://packslip.dev/docs/install/.
Run a command with
.B \-\-help
for its full help, or with
.B \-h
for a summary.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "install " PROJECT
Install a verified release and export its declared commands.
.TP
.BI "verify " BUNDLE
Verify a release bundle or release list, and each file given with
.BR \-\-artifact .
Nothing is downloaded.
.TP
.BI "pin " BUNDLE
Verify a release bundle and print its signer fingerprint.
.TP
.BI "show " BUNDLE
Print the statement inside a bundle without verifying it.
.TP
.BI "completion " SHELL
Print a shell completion script.
This package installs completions for bash, zsh, and fish.
.TP
.B version
Print packslip's version.
.SH INSTALL A TOOL
.I PROJECT
is
.IR owner/repo ,
.IR github.com/owner/repo [ /TOOL ],
or a domain project, one named after a host, such as
.IR mytool.example.com [ /PATH ].
A github.com project's releases are found on GitHub.
A domain project's releases are found in the signed release list its host
publishes.
gitlab.com projects are refused.
.PP
.B \-\-version
selects a version, prefix, range, or tag.
The default, latest, takes the vendor's recommended release, otherwise
the highest stable version.
When that release has no packslip for the project or no artifact for this
host, install warns and tries the next stable release.
Install never selects a release that the project's signed release list
withdraws, and warns when that list withdraws the release it last installed.
.B \-\-system
installs for all users and is the default for root on Unix.
.B \-\-user
installs for the current user, and root on Unix cannot select it.
.B \-\-install\-dir
and
.B \-\-bin\-dir
change where the tree and the commands go; trust state stays in the scope.
.B \-\-offline
uses only cached, authenticated metadata and artifacts.
.SH TRUST
A github.com project must be signed from its repository.
A keyless domain project's first install trusts the signer that its release
list and release bundle declare, fetched over HTTPS from that host.
A key-signed domain project needs
.B \-\-pubkey
on its first install, and later installs remember the key.
.PP
Later installs hold the project to what was accepted, and a keyless domain
project to the repository that signed it.
A changed signer or signing repository, keyless signing replaced by a key,
disabled workflow pinning, a repackager's bundle after the vendor's, or
dropped provenance needs
.B \-\-accept\-trust\-change
with the ID install printed for it.
A github.com name that now resolves to a different repository ID is refused.
.PP
.B \-\-pin
requires a signer fingerprint
.RI ( ps1_... )
that you obtained separately, such as from the project's README.
.BR \-\-issuer ,
.BR \-\-identity ,
and
.B \-\-identity\-prefix
narrow what the project's name requires and never replace it.
Administrator pins apply as well; see FILES.
.PP
.B \-\-force
replaces conflicting command entries and installation directories.
It never bypasses verification, trust-change approval, release list
freshness, the refusal of directories other users can write, or archive
limits.
Changes are staged, and an interrupted replacement is recovered before the
next install.
Once an install is committed, a cleanup failure is reported as a warning and
retried.
.SH VERIFY A RELEASE
A github.com or gitlab.com project's name sets the policy: the forge's
issuer, and a certificate whose source repository is the project's.
.BR \-\-issuer ,
.BR \-\-identity ,
and
.B \-\-identity\-prefix
narrow that policy and never replace it.
A domain project has no policy from its name, so pass
.B \-\-issuer
with
.BR \-\-identity ,
.BR \-\-identity\-prefix ,
.BR \-\-source\-repository ,
or
.BR \-\-pin .
.B \-\-pubkey
verifies a key-signed release instead.
After verification, check that the project and version are the ones you
meant.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the command succeeds, 1 when it fails, including when verify or pin
rejects a release, and 2 when the command line is invalid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR GH_TOKEN ", " GITHUB_TOKEN
A token for GitHub requests; GH_TOKEN wins when both are set.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Where a user install keeps its configuration, trees, and state, by default
~/.config, ~/.local/share, and ~/.local/state.
Root ignores them, HOME, and user configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/packslip/pins.d/*.toml
Administrator pins.
Each file that names the project adds a requirement no flag can remove.
.TP
.I ~/.config/packslip/pins.d/*.toml
A user's own pins, read by user installs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/packslip/config.toml
HTTP credentials for user installs, each scoped to one HTTPS origin.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/share/packslip/ ", " ~/.local/bin/ ", " ~/.local/state/packslip/
A user install's trees, commands, and state.
.TP
.IR /opt/packslip/ ", " /usr/local/bin/ ", " /var/lib/packslip/
A system install's trees, commands, and state.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/packslip/bootstrap.md
The bootstrap guide.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the latest release of hk:
.PP
.RS
packslip install github.com/jdx/hk
.RE
.PP
Install hk 2.8.0 and require its signer fingerprint:
.PP
.RS
.nf
packslip install github.com/jdx/hk \e
    \-\-version 2.8.0 \e
    \-\-pin ps1_snirenkjwr7m5ozgcufameodnm
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install a key-signed domain project:
.PP
.RS
packslip install mytool.example.com \-\-pubkey release.pub
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Bootstrap a tool: https://packslip.dev/docs/bootstrap/
.br
Verify a release: https://packslip.dev/docs/verifying/
.br
CLI reference: https://packslip.dev/cli/
